00:13:54.692 --> 00:14:17.873
Okay, so this is a little bit about Jung's views on science and something that I brought up very often, how Jung could, and in my eyes should be approached in his concept and his ideas. There's a certain parallelism to Einstein and how Einstein worked, because Einstein, super interesting person, super smart.

00:14:18.386 --> 00:14:41.745
Did amazing research. Well, did he do research? That's the thing. Einstein worked with a notepad and a pen. What he did was thought experiments saying, he said, oh, okay, when I'm riding a sled at the speed of light and I have a flashlight in my hand that's off and I turn it on, what happens? And he has that.

00:14:41.794 --> 00:15:03.138
He has a lot of thought experiments where he imagines himself In a kind of imaginary setting and thinks, okay, what would be the implications of that? So there's a lot of theory, there's a lot of thinking, there's not so much scientific research in the form of experiments on Einstein's part.

00:15:03.364 --> 00:15:22.710
