00:21:38.463 --> 00:21:59.649
And we start with a model of the psyche and one really fundamental thing about Jung and how he envisioned the psyche. And this is the research that he's done very early in his life. He checked how people react to stimuli words. Meaning he would give a word to a patient and they were supposed to give a kind of answer.

00:22:00.435 --> 00:22:21.049
And he would note down the answer and compare then people how they react to the same words. So he would take a group of people, give them the same word, and see how they would react differently. And what he've noticed that sometimes people would take a very long time to answer. And because he would run the experiment twice on the same person.

00:22:21.386 --> 00:22:42.773
They would not remember what the person said. And he said, okay, there's something weird. There's something going on. The person does react very slowly. So there's something in the back of their mind and they cannot remember it. So it's likely not from that person. And this was the basis for his ideas of complexes. And this is really a staple of psychoanalysis.

00:22:43.399 --> 00:23:08.988
And this has been proven to be correct that these words have an emotional effect on the person, and Jung went even further that they change something about our skin conductivity, meaning we bodily react to words and stimuli in an emotional way, but also completely bodily way.

00:23:09.309 --> 00:23:22.883
This is how lie detectors work, by the way. Jung laid there a lot of foundational work there. And this is very strongly proven and in line with what Jung worked in, in the beginning. So this is already nice to see.

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:48.585
Also, Jung came up with the terms of introversion and extraversion, meaning that people approach the world in a different way, either very outward looking or very inward looking. And these terms, completely scientifically valid. Used now, proven multiple times that people can be categorized like that, that they have a tendency to be more introverted or more extraverted.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:24:08.615
With a small caveat of saying, okay, it's today it's seen as a spectrum. That is not that you have 2 groups of people and you have the introverted people and the extraverted people. It's that you have specific types that are then very different from each other, but rather that everybody operates.

00:24:09.106 --> 00:24:32.980
On a kind of spectrum of where they land on different places, and you kind of have both. And here comes really the, let's say, hypothesizing further on findings. Jung laid this groundwork of complexes, but then described it as, okay, ah, complexes are kind of small personalities.

