Not all problems, but in general, it's a useful tool. That can be applied. Of course, there's many, many different tools in the repertoire of a psychologist or a therapist. Again, also I have to say here that I'm not a psychologist and I'm not a therapist, but the, there are different approaches like CBT, for example, that can help based on the problem of the patient.

